      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The authors report a case of myocardial infarction complicating an exercise stress test performed 48 hours after successful angioplasty of a stenosed left anterior descending artery in a patient with unstable angina. Three similar cases have been previously reported. The probable mechanisms of coronary obstruction in this context are rupture of an atheromatous plaque, thrombosis and coronary spasm."},
